      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think semantic versions make sense in this case? Semantic Versioning is about public API and backwards compatibility guarantees.\n\nThis JSON format is not intended to be a public API and promises zero backwards compatibility. Debug traces are ephemeral/kleenex. They exist as a way to transport semi-structured data out of C++ (SkVM/CanvasKit) and into Javascript (debugger-app-sk) at the moment the Debug button is clicked. The trace data only needs to exist for that brief moment in time.\n\nBackwards compatibility with JSON data from a different version isn\u0027t a planned feature because we don\u0027t have a use case for it. If version mismatches, we will reject the trace. \n\nVersion mismatches are only expected to happen when the Javascript and C++ code fall out of sync. The Javascript and C++ live in different repos, and CanvasKit updates require manual intervention, so sync issues are likely to occur occasionally and trigger a version-mismatch error. But the fix there is to update CanvasKit and re-push.",
